#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Quantum Optimization with Qiskit patterns {#3-quantum-optimization-with-qiskit-patterns}"
msgstr "3. Quantum Optimization gamit ang Qiskit Patterns {#3-quantum-optimization-with-qiskit-patterns}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this how-to we will learn about Qiskit patterns and quantum approximate optimization. A Qiskit pattern is an intuitive, repeatable set of steps for implementing a quantum computing workflow:\n"
"![\"Qiskit function\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/qiskit-function.avif)\n"
"We will apply the patterns to the context of **combinatorial optimization** and show how to solve the **max-cut** problem using the **Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA)**, a hybrid (quantum-classical) iterative method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa how-to na ito, matututunan natin ang tungkol sa Qiskit patterns at quantum approximate optimization. Ang Qiskit pattern ay isang intuitive at paulit-ulit na hanay ng mga hakbang para sa pagpapatupad ng quantum computing workflow:\n"
"![\"Qiskit function\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/qiskit-function.avif)\n"
"Ilalapat natin ang mga pattern sa konteksto ng **combinatorial optimization** at ipapakita kung paano solusyunan ang problemang **Max-Cut** gamit ang **Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA)**, isang hybrid (quantum-classical) na iterative na pamamaraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this QAOA part is based on \"Part 1: Small-scale QAOA\" of the [Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm) tutorial. See the tutorial to learn how to scale it up.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang bahaging QAOA na ito ay batay sa \"Part 1: Small-scale QAOA\" ng tutorial na [Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm). Tingnan ang tutorial para matutunan kung paano ito palawakin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 (Small-scale) Qiskit pattern for optimization {#31-small-scale-qiskit-pattern-for-optimization}"
msgstr "3.1 (Small-scale) Qiskit Pattern para sa Optimization {#31-small-scale-qiskit-pattern-for-optimization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This part will use a small-scale max-cut problem to illustrate the steps required to solve an optimization problem using a quantum computer.\n"
"The max-cut problem is an optimization problem that is hard to solve (more specifically, it is an NP-hard problem) with a number of different applications in clustering, network science, and statistical physics. This tutorial considers a graph of nodes connected by edges and aims to partition the nodes into two sets by \"cutting\" edges, such that the number of edges cut is maximized.\n"
"![\"Maxcut\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/maxcut.avif)\n"
"To give some context before mapping this problem to a quantum algorithm, you can better understand how the max-cut problem becomes a classical combinatorial optimization problem by first considering the minimization of a function $f(x)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagamitin ng bahaging ito ang isang maliit na Max-Cut na problema para ilarawan ang mga hakbang na kailangan para malutas ang isang optimization problem gamit ang quantum computer.\n"
"Ang Max-Cut na problema ay isang optimization problem na mahirap solusyunan (mas tiyak, isa itong NP-hard na problema) na may iba't ibang aplikasyon sa clustering, network science, at statistical physics. Isinasaalang-alang ng tutorial na ito ang isang graph ng mga node na konektado ng mga edge at layunin nitong hatiin ang mga node sa dalawang grupo sa pamamagitan ng \"pagputol\" ng mga edge, upang mapakinabangan ang bilang ng mga edge na naaputol.\n"
"![\"Maxcut\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/maxcut.avif)\n"
"Para magbigay ng konteksto bago i-map ang problemang ito sa isang quantum algorithm, mas mauunawaan mo kung paano nagiging classical combinatorial optimization problem ang Max-Cut sa pamamagitan ng pagsasaalang-alang muna ng minimization ng isang function na $f(x)$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}f(x),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}f(x),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the input $x$ is a vector whose components correspond to each node of a graph.  Then, constrain each of these components to be either $0$ or $1$ (which represent being included or not included in the cut). This small-scale example case uses a graph with $n=5$ nodes.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang input na $x$ ay isang vector na ang mga bahagi ay naaayon sa bawat node ng isang graph. Pagkatapos, pigilan ang bawat bahagi na maging alinman sa $0$ o $1$ (na kumakatawan sa pagiging kasama o hindi kasama sa cut). Ang maliit na halimbawang ito ay gumagamit ng graph na may $n=5$ na node.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You could write a function of a pair of nodes $i,j$ which indicates whether the corresponding edge $(i,j)$ is in the cut. For example, the function $x_i + x_j - 2 x_i x_j$ is 1 only if one of either $x_i$ or $x_j$ are 1 (which means that the edge is in the cut) and zero otherwise. The problem of maximizing the edges in the cut can be formulated as\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang sumulat ng function para sa isang pares ng mga node na $i,j$ na nagpapahiwatig kung ang kaukulang edge na $(i,j)$ ay nasa cut. Halimbawa, ang function na $x_i + x_j - 2 x_i x_j$ ay 1 lamang kung isa sa $x_i$ o $x_j$ ay 1 (na nangangahulugang ang edge ay nasa cut) at zero kung hindi. Ang problema ng pagpapakinabang ng mga edge sa cut ay maaaring buuin bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)} x_i + x_j - 2 x_i x_j,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)} x_i + x_j - 2 x_i x_j,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which can be rewritten as a minimization of the form\n"
msgstr "na maaaring isulat muli bilang isang minimization na may anyo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)}  2 x_i x_j - x_i - x_j.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)}  2 x_i x_j - x_i - x_j.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The minimum of $f(x)$ in this case is when the number of edges traversed by the cut is maximal. As you can see, there is nothing relating to quantum computing yet. You need to reformulate this problem into something that a quantum computer can understand.\n"
"Initialize your problem by creating a graph with $n=5$ nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang minimum ng $f(x)$ sa kasong ito ay kapag ang bilang ng mga edge na tinatagos ng cut ay pinakamataas. Tulad ng nakikita mo, wala pang kaugnayan sa quantum computing. Kailangan mong baguhin ang formulasyon ng problemang ito sa isang bagay na mauunawaan ng quantum computer.\n"
"Simulan ang iyong problema sa pamamagitan ng paglikha ng graph na may $n=5$ na node.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/extracted-outputs/99e763fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/extracted-outputs/99e763fe-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Step 1. Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#32-step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "3.2 Hakbang 1. I-map ang mga Classical Input sa isang Quantum Problem {#32-step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first step of the pattern is to map the classical problem (graph) into quantum **circuits** and **operators**. To do this, there are three main steps to take:\n"
msgstr "Ang unang hakbang ng pattern ay ang pag-map ng classical na problema (graph) sa mga quantum **circuit** at **operator**. Para magawa ito, may tatlong pangunahing hakbang na dapat sundin:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Utilize a series of mathematical reformulations, to represent this problem using the Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) problems notation.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ng serye ng mga mathematical reformulation para katawanin ang problemang ito gamit ang notasyon ng Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rewrite the optimization problem as a Hamiltonian for which the ground state corresponds to the solution which minimizes the cost function.\n"
msgstr "Isulat muli ang optimization problem bilang isang Hamiltonian na ang ground state ay naaayon sa solusyon na nagpapababa ng cost function.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a quantum circuit which will prepare the ground state of this Hamiltonian via a process similar to quantum annealing.\n"
msgstr "Lumikha ng quantum circuit na maghahanda ng ground state ng Hamiltoniang ito sa pamamagitan ng isang prosesong katulad ng quantum annealing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Note:** In the QAOA methodology, you ultimately want to have an operator (**Hamiltonian**) that represents the **cost function** of our hybrid algorithm, as well as a parametrized circuit (**Ansatz**) that represents quantum states with candidate solutions to the problem. You can sample from these candidate states and then evaluate them using the cost function.\n"
msgstr "**Tandaan:** Sa metodolohiya ng QAOA, ang layunin mo sa huli ay magkaroon ng isang operator (**Hamiltonian**) na kumakatawan sa **cost function** ng ating hybrid algorithm, pati na rin ang isang parametrized circuit (**Ansatz**) na kumakatawan sa mga quantum state na may mga candidate na solusyon sa problema. Maaari kang mag-sample mula sa mga candidate na state na ito at pagkatapos ay suriin ang mga ito gamit ang cost function.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Graph &rarr; optimization problem {#graph-optimization-problem}"
msgstr "Graph &rarr; optimization problem {#graph-optimization-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first step of the mapping is a notation change, The following expresses the problem in QUBO notation:\n"
msgstr "Ang unang hakbang ng mapping ay isang pagbabago ng notasyon. Ang sumusunod ay nagpapahayag ng problema sa QUBO notation:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}x^T Q x,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}x^T Q x,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $Q$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix of real numbers, $n$ corresponds to the number of nodes in your graph, $x$ is the vector of binary variables introduced above, and $x^T$ indicates the transpose of the vector $x$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $Q$ ay isang $n\\times n$ na matrix ng mga tunay na numero, ang $n$ ay naaayon sa bilang ng mga node sa iyong graph, ang $x$ ay ang vector ng mga binary variable na ipinakilala sa itaas, at ang $x^T$ ay nagpapahiwatig ng transpose ng vector na $x$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization problem &rarr; Hamiltonian {#optimization-problem-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Optimization problem &rarr; Hamiltonian {#optimization-problem-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can then reformulate the QUBO problem as a **Hamiltonian** (here, a matrix that represents the energy of a system):\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo ring baguhin ang formulasyon ng QUBO problem bilang isang **Hamiltonian** (dito, isang matrix na kumakatawan sa enerhiya ng isang sistema):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_C=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i b_iZ_i.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_C=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i b_iZ_i.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reformulation steps from the QAOA problem to the Hamiltonian**\n"
msgstr "**Mga hakbang ng reformulation mula sa QAOA problem patungong Hamiltonian**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To demonstrate how the QAOA problem can be rewritten in this way, first replace the binary variables $x_i$ to a new set of variables $z_i\\in\\{-1, 1\\}$ via\n"
msgstr "Para ipakita kung paano maisusulat muli ang QAOA problem sa ganitong paraan, palitan muna ang mga binary variable na $x_i$ ng isang bagong hanay ng mga variable na $z_i\\in\\{-1, 1\\}$ sa pamamagitan ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here you can see that if $x_i$ is $0$, then $z_i$ must be $1$. When the $x_i$'s are substituted for the $z_i$'s in the optimization problem ($x^TQx$), an equivalent formulation can be obtained.\n"
msgstr "Makikita dito na kung ang $x_i$ ay $0$, ang $z_i$ ay dapat na $1$. Kapag pinalitan ang mga $x_i$ ng $z_i$ sa optimization problem ($x^TQx$), maaaring makuha ang isang katumbas na formulasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x^TQx=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}x_ix_j \\\\ =\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}(1-z_i)(1-z_j) \\\\=\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}z_iz_j-\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})z_i + \\frac{n^2}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x^TQx=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}x_ix_j \\\\ =\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}(1-z_i)(1-z_j) \\\\=\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}z_iz_j-\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})z_i + \\frac{n^2}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now if we define $b_i=-\\sum_{j}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})$, remove the prefactor, and the constant $n^2$ term, we arrive at the two equivalent formulations of the same optimization problem.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon kung tukuyin natin ang $b_i=-\\sum_{j}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})$, alisin ang prefactor, at ang constant na $n^2$ na term, maaabot natin ang dalawang katumbas na formulasyon ng parehong optimization problem.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"min_{x\\in\\{0,1\\}^n} x^TQx\\Longleftrightarrow \\min_{z\\in\\{-1,1\\}^n}z^TQz + b^Tz\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"min_{x\\in\\{0,1\\}^n} x^TQx\\Longleftrightarrow \\min_{z\\in\\{-1,1\\}^n}z^TQz + b^Tz\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $b$ depends on $Q$. Note that to obtain $z^TQz + b^Tz$ we dropped the factor of 1/4 and a constant offset of $n^2$ which do not play a role in the optimization.\n"
msgstr "Dito, ang $b$ ay nakasalalay sa $Q$. Tandaan na para makuha ang $z^TQz + b^Tz$ inalis natin ang factor na 1/4 at isang constant offset na $n^2$ na hindi gumaganap ng papel sa optimization.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, to obtain a quantum formulation of the problem, promote the $z_i$ variables to a Pauli $Z$ matrix, such as a $2\\times 2$ matrix of the form\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, para makuha ang quantum formulation ng problema, i-promote ang mga variable na $z_i$ sa isang Pauli $Z$ matrix, tulad ng isang $2\\times 2$ na matrix na may anyo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
" $$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
" $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you substitute these matrices in the optimization problem above, you obtain the following Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr "Kapag pinalitan mo ang mga matrix na ito sa optimization problem sa itaas, makukuha mo ang sumusunod na Hamiltonian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Also recall that the $Z$ matrices are embedded in the quantum computer's computational space, that is, a Hilbert space of size $2^n\\times 2^n$. Therefore, you should understand terms such as $Z_iZ_j$ as the tensor product $Z_i\\otimes Z_j$ embedded in the $2^n\\times 2^n$ Hilbert space. For example, in a problem with five decision variables the term $Z_1Z_3$ is understood to mean $I\\otimes Z_3\\otimes I\\otimes Z_1\\otimes I$ where $I$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix.*\n"
msgstr "*Tandaan din na ang mga $Z$ matrix ay naka-embed sa computational space ng quantum computer, iyon ay, isang Hilbert space na may sukat na $2^n\\times 2^n$. Samakatuwid, dapat maunawaan ang mga term tulad ng $Z_iZ_j$ bilang ang tensor product na $Z_i\\otimes Z_j$ na naka-embed sa $2^n\\times 2^n$ na Hilbert space. Halimbawa, sa isang problema na may limang decision variable, ang term na $Z_1Z_3$ ay nangangahulugang $I\\otimes Z_3\\otimes I\\otimes Z_1\\otimes I$ kung saan ang $I$ ay ang $2\\times 2$ na identity matrix.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This Hamiltonian is called the <b>cost function Hamiltonian</b>. It has the property that its ground state corresponds to the solution that <b>minimizes the cost function $f(x)$</b>.\n"
"Therefore, to solve your optimization problem you now need to prepare the ground state of $H_C$ (or a state with a high overlap with it) on the quantum computer. Then, sampling from this state will, with a high probability, yield the solution to $\\min~f(x)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Hamiltonianing ito ay tinatawag na <b>cost function Hamiltonian</b>. Mayroon itong katangian na ang ground state nito ay naaayon sa solusyon na <b>nagpapababa ng cost function na $f(x)$</b>.\n"
"Samakatuwid, para malutas ang iyong optimization problem kailangan mo na ngayong ihanda ang ground state ng $H_C$ (o isang state na may mataas na overlap nito) sa quantum computer. Pagkatapos, ang pag-sample mula sa state na ito ay magbibigay, na may mataas na posibilidad, ng solusyon sa $\\min~f(x)$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian &rarr; quantum circuit {#hamiltonian-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian &rarr; quantum circuit {#hamiltonian-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian $H_C$ contains the quantum definition of your problem. Now you can create a quantum circuit that will help *sample* good solutions from the quantum computer. The QAOA is inspired by quantum annealing and applies alternating layers of operators in the quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang Hamiltonian na $H_C$ ay naglalaman ng quantum na kahulugan ng iyong problema. Ngayon ay maaari kang lumikha ng quantum circuit na tutulong sa *pag-sample* ng magagandang solusyon mula sa quantum computer. Ang QAOA ay inspirado ng quantum annealing at nag-aapply ng mga alternating layer ng mga operator sa quantum circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The general idea is to start in the ground state of a known system, $H^{\\otimes n}|0\\rangle$ above, and then steer the system into the ground state of the cost operator that you are interested in. This is done by applying the operators $\\exp\\{-i\\gamma_k H_C\\}$ and $\\exp\\{-i\\beta_k H_m\\}$ with angles $\\gamma_1,...,\\gamma_p$ and $\\beta_1,...,\\beta_p~$.\n"
msgstr "Ang pangkalahatang ideya ay magsimula sa ground state ng isang kilalang sistema, $H^{\\otimes n}|0\\rangle$ sa itaas, at pagkatapos ay gabayan ang sistema patungo sa ground state ng cost operator na interesado ka. Ginagawa ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng mga operator na $\\exp\\{-i\\gamma_k H_C\\}$ at $\\exp\\{-i\\beta_k H_m\\}$ na may mga anggulo na $\\gamma_1,...,\\gamma_p$ at $\\beta_1,...,\\beta_p~$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The quantum circuit that you generate is **parametrized** by $\\gamma_i$ and $\\beta_i$, so you can try out different values of $\\gamma_i$ and $\\beta_i$ and sample from the resulting state.\n"
"![\"QAOA circuit diagram\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/circuit-diagram.svg)\n"
"In this case we will try an example with 1 QAOA layer that contains two parameters: $\\gamma_1$ and $\\beta_1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang quantum circuit na iyong ginagawa ay **parametrized** ng $\\gamma_i$ at $\\beta_i$, kaya maaari kang subukan ang iba't ibang halaga ng $\\gamma_i$ at $\\beta_i$ at mag-sample mula sa resultang state.\n"
"![\"QAOA circuit diagram\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/circuit-diagram.svg)\n"
"Sa kasong ito, susubukan natin ang isang halimbawa na may 1 QAOA layer na naglalaman ng dalawang parameter: $\\gamma_1$ at $\\beta_1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/extracted-outputs/7bd8c6d4-f40f-4a11-a440-0b26d9021b53-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/extracted-outputs/7bd8c6d4-f40f-4a11-a440-0b26d9021b53-0.avif)\n"

